# The runtime environment of the GC stress workflow's "concurrent" build (.github/workflows/gc-stress.yml): Mono's
# concurrent mark-and-sweep collector, which TabStudio turned off (AndroidEnableSGenConcurrent in
# src/TabStudio.Android/TabStudio.Android.csproj), checking its own invariants. It reproduces the runtime race that
# made TabStudio abort in the collector: the concurrent mark reads object headers the Java GC bridge has tagged,
# loses a mod-union card and aborts with "major->major reference ... not found in remsets" (or crashes on the SGen
# worker thread without the checks). Run it to see whether a new .NET runtime has fixed the race; until then this
# build is expected to fail.
#
# Build it yourself with:
#   dotnet publish src/TabStudio.Android -c Release -f net10.0-android -p:TabStudioAndroidEnvironment=build/android/gc-stress/concurrent.env
#
# A 1 MB nursery (the default is 4 MB) makes minor collections, and with them the bridge's walks during a
# concurrent mark, four times as frequent.
MONO_GC_PARAMS=major=marksweep-conc,nursery-size=1m

# check-concurrent             checks the nursery around every concurrent collection, and clears it at each one.
# mod-union-consistency-check  before a concurrent collection finishes, every reference stored into an object the
#                              collector already marked must be in its mod-union cards, or it would be missed; a
#                              failure names the object's class and the reference's offset.
# clear-at-gc                  clears the nursery at each collection, so a stale pointer reads zeros.
# (check-mark-bits cannot run with the concurrent collector: building the nursery's fragments clears the pins just
# before it asserts that everything left in the nursery is pinned, so it aborts at the first major collection.)
MONO_GC_DEBUG=check-concurrent,mod-union-consistency-check,clear-at-gc
